##### Tie-order variation (present on base, not caused by the PR)

Every one of the 11 diary runs whose exact order differs has its first mismatch at position 92, and in every run the candidate set and the sort-key sequence match. The pair that swaps is `memory/2026-09-21.md:790-813` and `memory/2026-09-21.md:810-833`. In the frozen store both have the identical sort key:

```
memory/2026-09-21.md:790-813  lastRecalledAt=2026-10-04T06:33:40.129Z recallCount=21
memory/2026-09-21.md:810-833  lastRecalledAt=2026-10-04T06:33:40.129Z recallCount=21
```

`prepareLightDreaming` sorts by `lastRecalledAt` then `recallCount`, so with an exact tie the final order is the order in which the store hands the entries over, and `dedupeEntries` keeps first-seen order on both builds (compared side by side at the two commits). That input order varies between gateway runs: base shows the variation too (4 of 17 diary runs; REM evidence ordering 5 of 17; no-diary REM report 1 of 3 base runs). Head shows it in 7 of 17. With 17 runs per side that difference is within what chance gives (two-sided Fisher exact test on 4 of 17 versus 7 of 17: p = 0.4646, exactly 18797/40455, by enumerating the hypergeometric table; one-sided p = 0.2323), and the PR does not touch the store read path, but I cannot rule out a small skew with this sample, so I am stating the counts rather than hiding them. The deterministic CLI path (section 2) has no such variation, and there base and head are identical in all 8 runs.

