## Summary
- Retry a known-null settlement-store update once, only while the same exact OAuth refresh claim remains current.
- Preserve the validated replacement; never repeat the provider refresh or replay an unknown SQLite commit.
- Keep new claims, reconnects, failed fences, profile deletion, identity validation and custody checks authoritative.

Refs #166288. Only the transient known-null slice is addressed; this does not claim to solve hard owner termination, permanent I/O failures, or the historical production incident.

## Scope and related work
Two public files: the existing OAuth settlement owner and a focused regression module. No new API, configuration, marker format, dependency or background owner. #155369 protects graceful retirement; #152426 retries model-selection reads; #102438 is prior CAS-loss work, not permission to force-write over a newer same-account reconnect.

## Validation
Fresh base `f368d655393c9c28bff1646fc03462ae9492b119`; relevant auth/storage source seams match the earlier proof input. Dependencies were freshly installed from this head’s frozen lockfile.
Four relevant native files: 58 tests passed, 213.13 seconds wall under one worker and a constrained isolated Linux host. The added 11-case module uses actual auth-store settlement to prove persisted generation precedence; these cases cannot be reduced to a pure callback mock. CI seconds will be updated from the remote run.
The refreshed-base real SQLite/HTTP witness also passed: 1 test, 23.33 seconds wall, 12.3 seconds test time. The temporary witness is intentionally not added to routine CI; full source and manual steps follow.

## Real behavior proof
This does not attribute a production incident or establish recovery from permanent storage failure.

- **Behavior addressed:** Preserve an already validated OAuth replacement after a known-null store outcome, using at most two persistence attempts and a fresh exact-claim check. Do not repeat provider refresh or retry thrown outcome-unknown writes.
- **Real setup tested:** Current source at `660556970ac30cc71ee5b4a5bf8d270acc5a318a`, the real OAuth manager and real on-disk SQLite auth store, a separate `node:sqlite` connection holding `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, and a loopback HTTP OAuth stub with synthetic credentials only. The store call is pass-through instrumented for counting and to release the real holder after the actual null; no return value or SQLite failure is fabricated.
- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:** Publish the actual refresh claim, perform one POST to the loopback token endpoint, acquire the competing SQLite write lock after the provider returns, and let the real first settlement return null. Release the holder, allow the bounded second settlement, and read the persisted row. Run the identical fixture with unmodified and proposed source variants.
- **Evidence after fix:** Unpatched main fails with `Failed to persist refreshed OAuth credential`. Proposed source persists the validated replacement: one actual null, two owner-store attempts, one provider HTTP exchange. The test and native worker teardown both finish successfully; the loopback listener is closed. The first fixture attempt had a teardown-order failure and is not counted as a passing proof.
- **Observed result after fix:** The transient contention case recovers without another provider exchange. Native safety cases preserve newer owner/reconnect precedence, deleted profiles and failed fences, validator revocation, and no replay/terminalization of an unknown SQLite commit result. Adjacent OAuth tests: 58 passed. Type-aware lint: no warnings or errors after moving new tests into a focused module rather than disabling the file-length rule.
- **What was not tested:** A live OAuth provider, installed runtime, the historical incident's owner or write-stage identity, hard owner-worker termination, persistent I/O failure recovery, or every custody-retirement path. Runtime ownership remains enforced by the existing store admission and fresh validation; explicit retirement coverage still needs owner review.


Save the following temporary witness as `src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth-real-contention.proof.test.ts`, then run `pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.agents.config.ts src/agents/auth-profiles/oauth-real-contention.proof.test.ts --maxWorkers=1 --pool=forks`. Use synthetic state only, and remove the temporary source after verification once native teardown is complete.

<details><summary>Temporary Linux SQLite/HTTP witness</summary>

```ts
import fs from "node:fs/promises";
import http from "node:http";
import { execFileSync } from "node:child_process";
import { DatabaseSync } from "node:sqlite";
import path from "node:path";
import os from "node:os";
import { afterEach, expect, it, vi } from "vitest";
import { withEnvAsync } from "../../test-utils/env.js";
import { createOAuthRefreshCredential } from "./credential-fixtures.test-support.js";
import { createOAuthManager } from "./oauth-manager.js";
import { resolveAuthProfileDatabasePath } from "./sqlite.js";
import { loadPersistedAuthProfileStore } from "./persisted.js";
import * as storeRuntime from "./store-runtime.js";
afterEach(() => { vi.restoreAllMocks(); });
it("real SQLite contention after one loopback refresh preserves the rotated credential", async () => {
 const root=await fs.mkdtemp(path.join(os.tmpdir(),"oauth-real-contention-"));
 await withEnvAsync({OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR:root},async()=>{
  const agentDir=path.join(root,"agents","main","agent");await fs.mkdir(agentDir,{recursive:true});
  const profileId="xai:fixture";const old=createOAuthRefreshCredential({provider:"xai",access:"fixture-old-access",refresh:"fixture-old-refresh",expires:1,accountId:"fixture-account"});
  const replacement=createOAuthRefreshCredential({provider:"xai",access:"fixture-new-access",refresh:"fixture-new-refresh",expires:Date.now()+21600000,accountId:"fixture-account"});
  storeRuntime.saveAuthProfileStore({version:1,profiles:{[profileId]:old}},agentDir,{filterExternalAuthProfiles:false});
  let exchanges=0;let rotated=false;let holder:DatabaseSync|undefined;let writes=0;let actualNulls=0;
  const server=http.createServer((req,res)=>{if(req.url==="/health"){res.end("fixture-ready");return;}if(req.url!=="/token"||req.method!=="POST"){res.statusCode=404;res.end();return;}exchanges++;res.setHeader("Content-Type","application/json");res.end(JSON.stringify(replacement));});
  await new Promise<void>((resolve)=>server.listen(0,"localhost",resolve));
  const address=server.address();if(!address||typeof address==="string")throw new Error("No private listener address");
  const port=address.port;const listening=execFileSync("/usr/bin/ss",["-tlnpH"],{encoding:"utf8"});expect(listening.split(String.fromCharCode(10)).some((line)=>line.split(/\s+/u)[3]?.endsWith(":"+port)&&line.includes("pid="+process.pid+","))).toBe(true);
  const origin="http://localhost:"+port;expect(await(await fetch(origin+"/health")).text()).toBe("fixture-ready");
  const update=storeRuntime.updateAuthProfileStoreWithLock;
  // Pass-through instrumentation only: the real SQLite call supplies every result.
  vi.spyOn(storeRuntime,"updateAuthProfileStoreWithLock").mockImplementation(async(params)=>{
   if(rotated&&params.assertCurrent){writes++;const result=await update(params);if(result===null){actualNulls++;if(holder){holder.exec("ROLLBACK");holder.close();holder=undefined;}}return result;}
   return await update(params);
  });
  const adapter=vi.fn(async()=>{const response=await fetch(origin+"/token",{method:"POST"});if(!response.ok)throw new Error("Private provider rejected");const c=await response.json();holder=new DatabaseSync(resolveAuthProfileDatabasePath(agentDir));holder.exec("PRAGMA busy_timeout=0; BEGIN IMMEDIATE");rotated=true;return c;});
  const manager=createOAuthManager({buildApiKey:async(_p,c)=>c.access,canRefreshCredential:async()=>true,refreshCredential:adapter,readBootstrapCredential:()=>null});
  try{
   const result=await manager.resolveOAuthAccess({store:storeRuntime.ensureAuthProfileStoreWithoutExternalProfiles(agentDir),profileId,credential:old,agentDir});
   expect(result?.credential).toMatchObject(replacement);expect(actualNulls).toBe(1);expect(writes).toBe(2);expect(exchanges).toBe(1);expect(adapter).toHaveBeenCalledOnce();expect(loadPersistedAuthProfileStore(agentDir).profiles[profileId]).toMatchObject(replacement);
   console.log(JSON.stringify({proof:"real-store-contention",actualNulls,writes,providerExchanges:exchanges,sourceStoreUnmocked:true,rotatedCredentialPersisted:true}));
  }finally{if(holder){holder.exec("ROLLBACK");holder.close();}await new Promise<void>((resolve,reject)=>server.close(e=>e?reject(e):resolve()));expect(server.listening).toBe(false);}
 });
},90000);
```

</details>

## Standard entry-point status
The first standalone pnpm test invocation for the new module stopped before test execution (34.898 seconds wall). The filtered local dependency setup omitted quickjs-wasi, which the shared compiled-subprocess generation requires. No test ran in that attempt; it is not counted as a pass or a passing-file cost. Dependency reconciliation and the standard entry check are continuing. The 58 native direct-config cases and real-I/O witness above passed; CI and review readiness remain pending.

